GRID

-- Two columns either side of a fault with a full layer of throw: the columns
-- at I=3,4 sit one layer deeper than those at I=1,2. Each cell at I=2 then
-- faces nothing at all at I=3 in its own layer, and all of it at I=3 one layer
-- up, so every connection across the fault is one the grid works out from the
-- geometry. None of them is in the deck.
